make clean && make

Window 1 - manager
./manager 31500

Window 2 disk D1
./disk D1 127.0.0.1 31500 32001 32101
# register-disk D1 127.0.0.1 32001 32101

Window 3
./disk D2 127.0.0.1 31500 32002 32102
# register-disk D2 127.0.0.1 32002 32102

Window 4
./disk D3 127.0.0.1 31500 32003 32103
# register-disk D3 127.0.0.1 32003 32103

Window 5
./user user1 127.0.0.1 31500 31501 31551
# at the prompt:
register-user
# then:
configure-dss DSS1 3 1024

Window 6
./user user2 127.0.0.1 31500 31502 31552
# at the prompt:
register-user
# then (should FAIL due to no free disks):
configure-dss DSS2 3 1024

# in user1:
deregister-user
# in user2:
deregister-user
# (disks will refuse deregister while IN_DSS unless you implement destroy-dss)
# stop manager with Ctrl-C


recovery logic: For each drive in DSS except failed disk D = {0,1,...,n} \ {i}
For each file f stored on DSS:
  For each stripe j of file:
    Read block of stripe j from each disk in D in parallel
    Compute XOR of n-1 blocks and store as stripe j on drive i for f

First, we need to determine which files exist in this DSS
We'll query one of the working disks to get the file list

